  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two arrays AAA and BBB, both of length NNN.\n\nYou would like to choose **exactly** KKK **distinct** indices i1,i2,…,iKi_1,i_2, \\ldots, i_Ki1​,i2​,…,iK​ such that min⁡(Ai1+Ai2+…+AiK,Bi1+Bi2+…+BiK)\\min(A_{i_1}+A_{i_2}+ \\ldots + A_{i_K}, B_{i_1}+B_{i_2}+\\ldots + B_{i_K})min(Ai1​​+Ai2​​+…+AiK​​,Bi1​​+Bi2​​+…+BiK​​) is **maximized**. Find this maximum value.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nEach test case consists of 333 lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the elements of AAA.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​ denoting the elements of BBB.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a new line containing one integer — the required **maximum** value.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤201 \\leq T \\leq 201≤T≤20",
      "2≤N≤402 \\leq N \\leq 402≤N≤40",
      "1≤K≤N1 \\leq K \\leq N1≤K≤N",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤401 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 401≤Ai​,Bi​≤40"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n5 3\n4 2 3 1 4\n3 2 5 5 1\n4 2\n1 2 3 4\n4 3 2 1\n6 3\n8 10 3 6 7 2\n4 8 4 1 1 6",
        "output": "9\n5\n18",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: One optimal choice of indices is i1=1,i2=3,i3=5i_1 = 1, i_2 = 3, i_3 = 5i1​=1,i2​=3,i3​=5. This gives A1+A3+A5=11A_1 + A_3 + A_5 = 11A1​+A3​+A5​=11 and B1+B3+B5=9B_1 + B_3 + B_5 = 9B1​+B3​+B5​=9.\nTest Case 222: One optimal choice of indices is i1=1,i2=4i_1 = 1, i_2 = 4i1​=1,i2​=4.\nTest Case 333: One optimal choice of indices is i1=1,i2=2,i3=6i_1 = 1, i_2 = 2, i_3 = 6i1​=1,i2​=2,i3​=6."
      }
    ]
